<Prose bg="overview" title="Cookie policy" desc="GovPulse sets no analytics cookies by default. Google Analytics loads only after you accept in the consent banner. Cloudflare Web Analytics is cookieless." template>
<h2>No analytics cookies by default</h2>
<p>Browsing GovPulse does not set Google Analytics cookies unless you click Accept on the consent banner. We do not use advertising cookies, and we do not use session-replay tools that record keystrokes or page playback.</p>
<h2>Cloudflare Web Analytics</h2>
<p>If enabled, <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a> measures page views in aggregate without cookies and without fingerprinting.</p>
<h2>Google Analytics 4 (optional)</h2>
<p>When GA4 is configured, a consent banner appears on your first visit. Google Consent Mode v2 defaults to <code>analytics_storage: denied</code> (and ad-related storage denied). Analytics cookies (<code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code>, kept up to 2 years) are set only if you Accept. Declining is as easy as accepting — equal-weight buttons, no dark patterns. Your choice is stored in <code>localStorage</code> under <code>gp-consent</code>. Clear site data for this domain to be asked again.</p>
<p>GA4 enhanced measurement (if used) does not record keystrokes. We do not load Hotjar, Microsoft Clarity, FullStory, or similar session-replay products.</p>
<h2>Fonts</h2>
<p>Fonts are self-hosted. No requests go to <code>fonts.googleapis.com</code> or <code>fonts.gstatic.com</code>.</p>
<h2>No accounts</h2>
<p>GovPulse has no sign-in and no paid plans, so it uses no session or authentication cookies.</p>
<p>Last updated: 27 October 2026.</p>
</Prose>
